{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "t13-spawn-nonblocking-vs-delegate-blocking-upstream-order",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 5 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 5/L5): spawn_session's tool result returns the moment the child is registered, before the child's own turn does anything — proven by the parent immediately proceeding to a delegate_task call without ever waiting on the spawned child. delegate_task, in contrast, blocks: its own tool result is unreachable until every delegated child settles. Deterministic by construction, no gate on the parent's own progress: kidA (spawned, non-blocking) runs completely ungated and, once its own response naturally arrives, opens kidB's gate — kidB (delegated, blocking) is gated and can only resolve after that. The parent's own final text is therefore only reachable through the full causal chain kidA-responds -> kidB's gate opens -> kidB responds -> delegate_task resolves, which is only possible if delegate_task genuinely blocked on kidB while spawn_session genuinely did not block on kidA.",
